2026-10-19T19:59:45.151+08:00  INFO 5672 --- [phil-demo] [       Thread-1] c.iflytek.hy.service.SearchProxyService  : 大搜搜索接口原始返回: {"header":{"code":0,"traceId":"test-8718f027-b467-4ac6-a944-0988943cc441","message":"success","appId":"qctnk4ih"},"payload":{"output":{"data":[{"query":"check my bill","type":"raw","extra":[],"docs":[{"_indexCode":"PLDTRPAI_IDX_E15MHVUK","_indexName":"PLDT_data(PLDT_data)","_rank_index":1,"_rank_score":0.017635481,"_semtrc_index":7,"_semtrc_score":0.002491899,"_spanIds":[{"score":0.0024619582,"si":4,"text":"PLDT and Smart promote digital payment channels for customers\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\n“There’s a bonus. Online payments are greener,” she added. Enhanced digital channels\nSmart Postpaid customers can settle their bills at the safety of their homes by simply clicking the unique Smart Pay Express Link in the monthly billing SMS that they receive on their smartphones. They can also log on to www.my.smart.com.ph using their My Smart account to pay their phone bills.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.002391374,"si":6,"text":"PLDT and Smart promote digital payment channels for customers\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nFor the more tech-savvy subscribers, they can download and use digital payments app PayMaya to pay their Smart Postpaid bill or buy load for their devices. PayMaya is currently offering a P50 rebate for PLDT, Smart and Sun postpaid accounts until July 31.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.002279274,"si":0,"text":"PLDT and Smart promote digital payment channels for customers\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nAdvisories PLDT and Smart promote digital payment channels for customers Jul 23, 2020 PLDT and its wireless subsidiary Smart Communications, Inc (Smart) are encouraging their subscribers to use their expanded digital payment channels and online billing services, not only because these are more convenient and safe during the COVID-19 pandemic, but also because these processes are","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0022512614,"si":2,"text":"PLDT and Smart promote digital payment channels for customers\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nmore environment-friendly. The shift to paperless transactions is already underway as customer payments via digital channels have jumped three-fold compared to last year, particularly after many parts of the country were placed under quarantine in mid-March of this year. “The health and safety of our customers are our priority.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0022390427,"si":13,"text":"PLDT and Smart promote digital payment channels for customers\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nFor more information, visit smrt.ph/apc. RELATED ARTICLES Advisories PLDT cable cut advisory Oct. 2, 2026 Oct 2, 2026 Advisories PLDT, Smart Inday, habagat advisory Jul 8, 2026 Advisories PLDT, Smart Mindanao earthquake advisory Jun 9, 2026 Advisories PLDT, Smart ‘Mayon’ advisory May 6, 2026 Advisories PLDT, Smart #UwanPH Advisory Nov 8, 2025 LATEST ARTICLES News Subsea cables are","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0022353933,"si":3,"text":"PLDT and Smart promote digital payment channels for customers\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\n“The health and safety of our customers are our priority. By using our online payment channels, our customers do not have to physically go to our stores to pay their bill. It saves them time, money, and at the same time, protects them from possible exposure to COVID-19,” said Jane J. Basas, SVP and Head of Consumer Wireless Business at Smart. “There’s a bonus.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0022254884,"si":10,"text":"PLDT and Smart promote digital payment channels for customers\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nGoing green\nCustomers are also encouraged to enroll to electronic statements for a more convenient and environment-friendly lifestyle. “We also hope that by shifting to digital payments, we can help promote more paperless transactions, and lesser carbon footprint among our subscribers,” said Basas.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.002218604,"si":9,"text":"PLDT and Smart promote digital payment channels for customers\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nMVP Rewards App users can also redeem bill credits, which can be used to settle their Smart postpaid bill. On the other hand, customers may also drop by the nearest accredited partner establishments, like 7-Eleven, The SM Store, Robinsons, Bayad Center, Cebuana Lhuillier, ECPay and others, to pay their monthly subscription bills.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0021741993,"si":12,"text":"PLDT and Smart promote digital payment channels for customers\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nThis is on top of the various climate change mitigation programs to help protect and conserve rainforests, mangroves and marine life — all leveraging on digital technology and the data networks of PLDT and Smart. For more information, visit smrt.ph/apc.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0021576495,"si":8,"text":"PLDT and Smart promote digital payment channels for customers\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nMoreover, they can also use the bills payment services of banks — such as those of Asia United Bank, BancNet, BDO, BPI, EastWest, Landbank, Maybank, Metrobank, PNB, PSBank, Robinsons Bank, Security Bank, UCPB and Union Bank — via their respective mobile apps, internet or phone banking services.","type":"semt"}],"_x":{"a":1,"at":1792049596290,"au":"System","cts":1792043917010,"df":0,"op":1,"sbc":"PLDTRPAI_WEB_DLFTHNSX","srcId":2110611279747141633,"uts":1792049596290,"v":0},"content":"Advisories\nPLDT and Smart promote digital payment channels for customers\nJul 23, 2020\nPLDT and its wireless subsidiary Smart Communications, Inc (Smart) are encouraging their subscribers to use their expanded digital payment channels and online billing services, not only because these are more convenient and safe during the COVID-19 pandemic, but also because these processes are more environment-friendly.\nThe shift to paperless transactions is already underway as customer payments via digital channels have jumped three-fold compared to last year, particularly after many parts of the country were placed under quarantine in mid-March of this year.\n“The health and safety of our customers are our priority. By using our online payment channels, our customers do not have to physically go to our stores to pay their bill. It saves them time, money, and at the same time, protects them from possible exposure to COVID-19,” said Jane J. Basas, SVP and Head of Consumer Wireless Business at Smart.\n“There’s a bonus. Online payments are greener,” she added.\nEnhanced digital channels\nSmart Postpaid customers can settle their bills at the safety of their homes by simply clicking the unique Smart Pay Express Link in the monthly billing SMS that they receive on their smartphones. They can also log on to www.my.smart.com.ph using their My Smart account to pay their phone bills.\nMeanwhile, PLDT customers can also go to https://pldthome.com/paymentcenters and click on the PLDT Pay Express Link for their transactions.\nFor customers with credit cards, they can enroll their postpaid account in their credit card’s auto-debit feature.\nFor the more tech-savvy subscribers, they can download and use digital payments app PayMaya to pay their Smart Postpaid bill or buy load for their devices. PayMaya is currently offering a P50 rebate for PLDT, Smart and Sun postpaid accounts until July 31.\nCustomers can also purchase call, text and data credits online via the Smart Online Store, and official platforms such as Lazada, Shopee, Grab and others.\nMoreover, they can also use the bills payment services of banks — such as those of Asia United Bank, BancNet, BDO, BPI, EastWest, Landbank, Maybank, Metrobank, PNB, PSBank, Robinsons Bank, Security Bank, UCPB and Union Bank — via their respective mobile apps, internet or phone banking services.\nMVP Rewards App users can also redeem bill credits, which can be used to settle their Smart postpaid bill.\nOn the other hand, customers may also drop by the nearest accredited partner establishments, like 7-Eleven, The SM Store, Robinsons, Bayad Center, Cebuana Lhuillier, ECPay and others, to pay their monthly subscription bills.\nGoing green\nCustomers are also encouraged to enroll to electronic statements for a more convenient and environment-friendly lifestyle.\n“We also hope that by shifting to digital payments, we can help promote more paperless transactions, and lesser carbon footprint among our subscribers,” said Basas.\nPLDT and Smart are committed to become carbon neutral before 2030 by conducting business more responsibly and resiliently. The Group aims to do this by progressively improving operational efficiencies, turning to green technologies and processes and pursuing the use of renewable energy in its facilities.\nThis is on top of the various climate change mitigation programs to help protect and conserve rainforests, mangroves and marine life — all leveraging on digital technology and the data networks of PLDT and Smart.\nFor more information, visit smrt.ph/apc.\nRELATED ARTICLES\nAdvisories\nPLDT cable cut advisory Oct. 2, 2026\nOct 2, 2026\nAdvisories\nPLDT, Smart Inday, habagat advisory\nJul 8, 2026\nAdvisories\nPLDT, Smart Mindanao earthquake advisory\nJun 9, 2026\nAdvisories\nPLDT, Smart ‘Mayon’ advisory\nMay 6, 2026\nAdvisories\nPLDT, Smart #UwanPH Advisory\nNov 8, 2025\nLATEST ARTICLES\nNews\nSubsea cables are critical infra requiring whole-of-nation protection – PLDT\nOct 14, 2026\nMalasakit (ESG)\nPLDT, Smart and Unilab Foundation bring crisis-tested learning program to more Philippine schools\nOct 13, 2026\nNews\nPLDT Global and Smart extend support to Filipinos in Saudi Arabia amid ongoing incident\nOct 13, 2026\nNews\nPLDT Group’s ERICA Wins 2026 AIBP Enterprise Innovation Award for Data and AI\nOct 9, 2026","domain":"main.pldt.com","id":2110626005457707008,"post_ts":1595433600000,"ss":[{"chunk_id":0,"content":"Advisories PLDT and Smart promote digital payment channels for customers Jul 23, 2020 PLDT and its wireless subsidiary Smart Communications, Inc (Smart) are encouraging their subscribers to use their expanded digital payment channels and online billing services, not only because these are more convenient and safe during the COVID-19 pandemic, but also because these processes are","ctx":{"span":[0,380]}},{"chunk_id":1,"content":"more environment-friendly.","ctx":{"span":[0,25]}},{"chunk_id":2,"content":"more environment-friendly. The shift to paperless transactions is already underway as customer payments via digital channels have jumped three-fold compared to last year, particularly after many parts of the country were placed under quarantine in mid-March of this year. “The health and safety of our customers are our priority.","ctx":{"span":[0,328]}},{"chunk_id":3,"content":"“The health and safety of our customers are our priority. By using our online payment channels, our customers do not have to physically go to our stores to pay their bill. It saves them time, money, and at the same time, protects them from possible exposure to COVID-19,” said Jane J. Basas, SVP and Head of Consumer Wireless Business at Smart. “There’s a bonus.","ctx":{"span":[0,361]}},{"chunk_id":4,"content":"“There’s a bonus. Online payments are greener,” she added. Enhanced digital channels\nSmart Postpaid customers can settle their bills at the safety of their homes by simply clicking the unique Smart Pay Express Link in the monthly billing SMS that they receive on their smartphones. They can also log on to www.my.smart.com.ph using their My Smart account to pay their phone bills.","ctx":{"span":[0,379]}},{"chunk_id":5,"content":"Meanwhile, PLDT customers can also go to https://pldthome.com/paymentcenters and click on the PLDT Pay Express Link for their transactions. For customers with credit cards, they can enroll their postpaid account in their credit card’s auto-debit feature.","ctx":{"span":[0,253]}},{"chunk_id":6,"content":"For the more tech-savvy subscribers, they can download and use digital payments app PayMaya to pay their Smart Postpaid bill or buy load for their devices. PayMaya is currently offering a P50 rebate for PLDT, Smart and Sun postpaid accounts until July 31.","ctx":{"span":[0,254]}},{"chunk_id":7,"content":"Customers can also purchase call, text and data credits online via the Smart Online Store, and official platforms such as Lazada, Shopee, Grab and others.","ctx":{"span":[0,153]}},{"chunk_id":8,"content":"Moreover, they can also use the bills payment services of banks — such as those of Asia United Bank, BancNet, BDO, BPI, EastWest, Landbank, Maybank, Metrobank, PNB, PSBank, Robinsons Bank, Security Bank, UCPB and Union Bank — via their respective mobile apps, internet or phone banking services.","ctx":{"span":[0,294]}},{"chunk_id":9,"content":"MVP Rewards App users can also redeem bill credits, which can be used to settle their Smart postpaid bill. On the other hand, customers may also drop by the nearest accredited partner establishments, like 7-Eleven, The SM Store, Robinsons, Bayad Center, Cebuana Lhuillier, ECPay and others, to pay their monthly subscription bills.","ctx":{"span":[0,330]}},{"chunk_id":10,"content":"Going green\nCustomers are also encouraged to enroll to electronic statements for a more convenient and environment-friendly lifestyle. “We also hope that by shifting to digital payments, we can help promote more paperless transactions, and lesser carbon footprint among our subscribers,” said Basas.","ctx":{"span":[0,298]}},{"chunk_id":11,"content":"PLDT and Smart are committed to become carbon neutral before 2030 by conducting business more responsibly and resiliently. The Group aims to do this by progressively improving operational efficiencies, turning to green technologies and processes and pursuing the use of renewable energy in its facilities.","ctx":{"span":[0,304]}},{"chunk_id":12,"content":"This is on top of the various climate change mitigation programs to help protect and conserve rainforests, mangroves and marine life — all leveraging on digital technology and the data networks of PLDT and Smart. For more information, visit smrt.ph/apc.","ctx":{"span":[0,252]}},{"chunk_id":13,"content":"For more information, visit smrt.ph/apc. RELATED ARTICLES Advisories PLDT cable cut advisory Oct. 2, 2026 Oct 2, 2026 Advisories PLDT, Smart Inday, habagat advisory Jul 8, 2026 Advisories PLDT, Smart Mindanao earthquake advisory Jun 9, 2026 Advisories PLDT, Smart ‘Mayon’ advisory May 6, 2026 Advisories PLDT, Smart #UwanPH Advisory Nov 8, 2025 LATEST ARTICLES News Subsea cables are","ctx":{"span":[0,382]}},{"chunk_id":14,"content":"critical infra requiring whole-of-nation protection – PLDT Oct 14, 2026 Malasakit (ESG) PLDT, Smart and Unilab Foundation bring crisis-tested learning program to more Philippine schools Oct 13, 2026 News PLDT Global and Smart extend support to Filipinos in Saudi Arabia amid ongoing incident Oct 13, 2026 News PLDT Group’s ERICA Wins 2026 AIBP Enterprise Innovation Award for Data and","ctx":{"span":[0,383]}},{"chunk_id":15,"content":"AI Oct 9, 2026","ctx":{"span":[0,13]}}],"summary":"Official site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider","title":"PLDT and Smart promote digital payment channels for customers","url":"https://main.pldt.com/article/pldt-and-smart-promote-digital-payment-channels-customers"},{"_indexCode":"PLDTRPAI_IDX_E15MHVUK","_indexName":"PLDT_data(PLDT_data)","_rank_index":2,"_rank_score":0.00914112,"_semtrc_index":14,"_semtrc_score":0.0024628504,"_spanIds":[{"score":0.0023624657,"si":5,"text":"PLDT Global and its subsidiary, PLDT Online Inc., partners with Bayad Center to provide online bills payment facility for Overseas Filipinos\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nAs a special offer this holiday season, all online bills payments done until December 31, 2015 can enjoy a discounted transaction fee of only Php10.00. Simply log on to www.smartpinoystore.com to enjoy an easy, convenient and secure way of paying bills back home from anywhere around the world.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0022860547,"si":1,"text":"PLDT Global and its subsidiary, PLDT Online Inc., partners with Bayad Center to provide online bills payment facility for Overseas Filipinos\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\n(PGC), has recently partnered with Bayad Center to enable online bills payments for Overseas Filipinos worldwide. This partnership empowers Pinoys abroad to securely and conveniently manage and process their payables back home through an easy to use web-based payment facility.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.002252607,"si":2,"text":"PLDT Global and its subsidiary, PLDT Online Inc., partners with Bayad Center to provide online bills payment facility for Overseas Filipinos\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nAmong the accredited biller companies of Bayad Center are Meralco, Maynilad, Visayan Electric Company, Davao Light, PLDT, Bayantel, Digitel, Smart, Cignal, Manila Water, Laguna Water District, PAG-IBIG Fund and more.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0022387414,"si":6,"text":"PLDT Global and its subsidiary, PLDT Online Inc., partners with Bayad Center to provide online bills payment facility for Overseas Filipinos\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nThe Smart Pinoy Store is an online portal that allows overseas Filipinos to buy gifts for their loved ones back at home at flexible and secure payment options.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0022073186,"si":4,"text":"PLDT Global and its subsidiary, PLDT Online Inc., partners with Bayad Center to provide online bills payment facility for Overseas Filipinos\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\n“This Bayad Center online bills payment facility is one of the enhancements in the Smart Pinoy Store. With the addition of Bayad Center under Smart Pinoy Store, the online portal continues to expand its offerings while cementing its leadership as a one-stop overseas Pinoy retail store,” said PGC President Alex Caeg.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0022046587,"si":9,"text":"PLDT Global and its subsidiary, PLDT Online Inc., partners with Bayad Center to provide online bills payment facility for Overseas Filipinos\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nsupport to Filipinos in Saudi Arabia amid ongoing incident Oct 13, 2026 News PLDT Group’s ERICA Wins 2026 AIBP Enterprise Innovation Award for Data and AI Oct 9, 2026","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0021558104,"si":7,"text":"PLDT Global and its subsidiary, PLDT Online Inc., partners with Bayad Center to provide online bills payment facility for Overseas Filipinos\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nRELATED ARTICLES News Subsea cables are critical infra requiring whole-of-nation protection – PLDT Oct 14, 2026 News PLDT Global and Smart extend support to Filipinos in Saudi Arabia amid ongoing incident Oct 13, 2026 News PLDT Group’s ERICA Wins 2026 AIBP Enterprise Innovation Award for Data and AI Oct 9, 2026 News PLDT and Smart partner with Capillary to unify loyalty programs","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0021435267,"si":8,"text":"PLDT Global and its subsidiary, PLDT Online Inc., partners with Bayad Center to provide online bills payment facility for Overseas Filipinos\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nOct 5, 2026 News PLDT Global executive urges culture-first leadership in Hong Kong business forum Oct 2, 2026 LATEST ARTICLES News Subsea cables are critical infra requiring whole-of-nation protection – PLDT Oct 14, 2026 Malasakit (ESG) PLDT, Smart and Unilab Foundation bring crisis-tested learning program to more Philippine schools Oct 13, 2026 News PLDT Global and Smart extend","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0020979561,"si":3,"text":"PLDT Global and its subsidiary, PLDT Online Inc., partners with Bayad Center to provide online bills payment facility for Overseas Filipinos\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\n“We are relentless in our pursuit of improving the lives of our Overseas Filipinos, and this partnership will now allow them to directly and securely settle their typical family bills over the Internet, which is very similar to how they did it before – as if they never left home,\" said PLDT and Smart EVP and Head of Enterprise, International, and Carrier Business, Eric Alberto.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0020776426,"si":0,"text":"PLDT Global and its subsidiary, PLDT Online Inc., partners with Bayad Center to provide online bills payment facility for Overseas Filipinos\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nNews\nPLDT Global and its subsidiary, PLDT Online Inc., partners with Bayad Center to provide online bills payment facility for Overseas Filipinos\nJan 5, 2016\nMANILA, Philippines, December 9, 2015 – Leading telecommunication and digital services provider PLDT, through its International Marketing, Sales and Operating arm PLDT Global Corp.","type":"semt"}],"_x":{"a":1,"at":1792049593067,"au":"System","cts":1792043917585,"df":0,"op":1,"sbc":"PLDTRPAI_WEB_DLFTHNSX","srcId":2110611282158866433,"uts":1792049593067,"v":0},"content":"News\nPLDT Global and its subsidiary, PLDT Online Inc., partners with Bayad Center to provide online bills payment facility for Overseas Filipinos\nJan 5, 2016\nMANILA, Philippines, December 9, 2015 – Leading telecommunication and digital services provider PLDT, through its International Marketing, Sales and Operating arm PLDT Global Corp. (PGC), has recently partnered with Bayad Center to enable online bills payments for Overseas Filipinos worldwide.\nThis partnership empowers Pinoys abroad to securely and conveniently manage and process their payables back home through an easy to use web-based payment facility. Among the accredited biller companies of Bayad Center are Meralco, Maynilad, Visayan Electric Company, Davao Light, PLDT, Bayantel, Digitel, Smart, Cignal, Manila Water, Laguna Water District, PAG-IBIG Fund and more.\n“We are relentless in our pursuit of improving the lives of our Overseas Filipinos, and this partnership will now allow them to directly and securely settle their typical family bills over the Internet, which is very similar to how they did it before – as if they never left home,\" said PLDT and Smart EVP and Head of Enterprise, International, and Carrier Business, Eric Alberto.\n“This Bayad Center online bills payment facility is one of the enhancements in the Smart Pinoy Store. With the addition of Bayad Center under Smart Pinoy Store, the online portal continues to expand its offerings while cementing its leadership as a one-stop overseas Pinoy retail store,” said PGC President Alex Caeg.\nAs a special offer this holiday season, all online bills payments done until December 31, 2015 can enjoy a discounted transaction fee of only Php10.00. Simply log on to www.smartpinoystore.com to enjoy an easy, convenient and secure way of paying bills back home from anywhere around the world.\nThe Smart Pinoy Store is an online portal that allows overseas Filipinos to buy gifts for their loved ones back at home at flexible and secure payment options.\nRELATED ARTICLES\nNews\nSubsea cables are critical infra requiring whole-of-nation protection – PLDT\nOct 14, 2026\nNews\nPLDT Global and Smart extend support to Filipinos in Saudi Arabia amid ongoing incident\nOct 13, 2026\nNews\nPLDT Group’s ERICA Wins 2026 AIBP Enterprise Innovation Award for Data and AI\nOct 9, 2026\nNews\nPLDT and Smart partner with Capillary to unify loyalty programs\nOct 5, 2026\nNews\nPLDT Global executive urges culture-first leadership in Hong Kong business forum\nOct 2, 2026\nLATEST ARTICLES\nNews\nSubsea cables are critical infra requiring whole-of-nation protection – PLDT\nOct 14, 2026\nMalasakit (ESG)\nPLDT, Smart and Unilab Foundation bring crisis-tested learning program to more Philippine schools\nOct 13, 2026\nNews\nPLDT Global and Smart extend support to Filipinos in Saudi Arabia amid ongoing incident\nOct 13, 2026\nNews\nPLDT Group’s ERICA Wins 2026 AIBP Enterprise Innovation Award for Data and AI\nOct 9, 2026","domain":"main.pldt.com","id":2110626004845338624,"post_ts":1451923200000,"ss":[{"chunk_id":0,"content":"News\nPLDT Global and its subsidiary, PLDT Online Inc., partners with Bayad Center to provide online bills payment facility for Overseas Filipinos\nJan 5, 2016\nMANILA, Philippines, December 9, 2015 – Leading telecommunication and digital services provider PLDT, through its International Marketing, Sales and Operating arm PLDT Global Corp.","ctx":{"span":[0,337]}},{"chunk_id":1,"content":"(PGC), has recently partnered with Bayad Center to enable online bills payments for Overseas Filipinos worldwide. This partnership empowers Pinoys abroad to securely and conveniently manage and process their payables back home through an easy to use web-based payment facility.","ctx":{"span":[0,276]}},{"chunk_id":2,"content":"Among the accredited biller companies of Bayad Center are Meralco, Maynilad, Visayan Electric Company, Davao Light, PLDT, Bayantel, Digitel, Smart, Cignal, Manila Water, Laguna Water District, PAG-IBIG Fund and more.","ctx":{"span":[0,215]}},{"chunk_id":3,"content":"“We are relentless in our pursuit of improving the lives of our Overseas Filipinos, and this partnership will now allow them to directly and securely settle their typical family bills over the Internet, which is very similar to how they did it before – as if they never left home,\" said PLDT and Smart EVP and Head of Enterprise, International, and Carrier Business, Eric Alberto.","ctx":{"span":[0,379]}},{"chunk_id":4,"content":"“This Bayad Center online bills payment facility is one of the enhancements in the Smart Pinoy Store. With the addition of Bayad Center under Smart Pinoy Store, the online portal continues to expand its offerings while cementing its leadership as a one-stop overseas Pinoy retail store,” said PGC President Alex Caeg.","ctx":{"span":[0,316]}},{"chunk_id":5,"content":"As a special offer this holiday season, all online bills payments done until December 31, 2015 can enjoy a discounted transaction fee of only Php10.00. Simply log on to www.smartpinoystore.com to enjoy an easy, convenient and secure way of paying bills back home from anywhere around the world.","ctx":{"span":[0,293]}},{"chunk_id":6,"content":"The Smart Pinoy Store is an online portal that allows overseas Filipinos to buy gifts for their loved ones back at home at flexible and secure payment options.","ctx":{"span":[0,158]}},{"chunk_id":7,"content":"RELATED ARTICLES News Subsea cables are critical infra requiring whole-of-nation protection – PLDT Oct 14, 2026 News PLDT Global and Smart extend support to Filipinos in Saudi Arabia amid ongoing incident Oct 13, 2026 News PLDT Group’s ERICA Wins 2026 AIBP Enterprise Innovation Award for Data and AI Oct 9, 2026 News PLDT and Smart partner with Capillary to unify loyalty programs","ctx":{"span":[0,380]}},{"chunk_id":8,"content":"Oct 5, 2026 News PLDT Global executive urges culture-first leadership in Hong Kong business forum Oct 2, 2026 LATEST ARTICLES News Subsea cables are critical infra requiring whole-of-nation protection – PLDT Oct 14, 2026 Malasakit (ESG) PLDT, Smart and Unilab Foundation bring crisis-tested learning program to more Philippine schools Oct 13, 2026 News PLDT Global and Smart extend","ctx":{"span":[0,380]}},{"chunk_id":9,"content":"support to Filipinos in Saudi Arabia amid ongoing incident Oct 13, 2026 News PLDT Group’s ERICA Wins 2026 AIBP Enterprise Innovation Award for Data and AI Oct 9, 2026","ctx":{"span":[0,165]}}],"summary":"Official site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider","title":"PLDT Global and its subsidiary, PLDT Online Inc., partners with Bayad Center to provide online bills payment facility for Overseas Filipinos","url":"https://main.pldt.com/article/pldt-global-and-its-subsidiary-pldt-online-inc-partners-bayad-center-provide-online-bills"},{"_indexCode":"PLDTRPAI_IDX_E15MHVUK","_indexName":"PLDT_data(PLDT_data)","_rank_index":3,"_rank_score":0.007300106,"_textrecall_index":1,"_textrecall_score":75.11077,"_x":{"a":1,"at":1792049621674,"au":"System","cts":1792043916963,"df":0,"op":1,"sbc":"PLDTRPAI_WEB_DLFTHNSX","srcId":2110611279550009348,"uts":1792049621674,"v":0},"content":"News\nSmart, regulators revisit vetoed SIM registration bill, push for global best practices for consumer protection\nApr 21, 2022\nLeading mobile services provider Smart Communications, Inc. (Smart) will bring to the table its expertise and knowledge on global best practices as it continues to work with government to ensure consumer protection through measures like the SIM card registration bill.\nThis comes after the President's recent veto of the measure and reports of the Senate President's announcement of his plan to use Congress' power to override the veto.\n\"Smart has long been in the forefront of consumer online protection and has been actively pushing programs toward this pursuit. This includes initiatives that keep our customers safe from scams and fraud, activities that uphold the highest standards of data privacy, and programs that promote safe online spaces for all, especially for children,\" said Alfredo S. Panlilio, PLDT Inc and Smart Communications President and CEO.\n\"More than supporting the legislative process, we at Smart are also willing to share our own experiences, as well as our knowledge on the best global practices, to contribute to the success of the SIM card registration bill, if and when it is passed into law. We also welcome any opportunity to support the government in developing the bill's implementing rules and regulations,\" Panlilio added.\nSpeaking to reporters on the sidelines of PLDT's tower deal announcement, PLDT chair Manuel V. Pangilinan reiterated the company's support for the measure. \"We still are hoping that we will find a way to get the SIM cards registered. That's important, not only for our business, but for Filipinos in general.\"\nPLDT Chief Legal Counsel Marilyn V. Aquino also said: \"Before the veto, we were planning to work with regulators, and we were looking for best practices abroad, including rules and regulations that were adopted and how they were applied, including challenges encountered and mistakes that can be avoided. The plan is to work with regulators so that we can share information on what has happened as well as what is happening in other countries so that we don't make the same mistakes. That was the plan before the veto happened, and we will continue to do that.\"\nSmart and parent company PLDT have been active in collaborating with government and regulators for consumer protection. Through its Cybersecurity Operations Group, PLDT has invested billions to beef up its cybersecurity defenses, not only to protect its own infrastructure but mostly to help protect customers from cyberthreats and phishing and scamming activities. PLDT and Smart also regularly and actively campaign to inform and educate customers and help them identify red flags that indicate scams and fraud.\nPLDT and Smart have also embraced their role in the fight against online sexual abuse and exploitation of children (OSAEC) by rolling out relevant policies, technology solutions, and community programs that uphold the safety and welfare of children both online and offline. This includes investing in a pioneering Child Protection Platform and embedding it into the Group's 24/7 cyber security operations. This solution allows the Group to detect, predict, respond, and prevent domain and content-level access to child sexual abuse materials. As of end March 2022, PLDT and Smart have already blocked an accumulation of more than 1 billion user access attempts and over 224,000 online content and web pages linked to OSAEC.\nPLDT's Data Privacy Office has also been taking the lead in holding Group-wide data privacy trainings to equip leaders and employees alike as data privacy champions for customers.\nRELATED ARTICLES\nNews\nSubsea cables are critical infra requiring whole-of-nation protection – PLDT\nOct 14, 2026\nNews\nPLDT Global and Smart extend support to Filipinos in Saudi Arabia amid ongoing incident\nOct 13, 2026\nNews\nPLDT Group’s ERICA Wins 2026 AIBP Enterprise Innovation Award for Data and AI\nOct 9, 2026\nNews\nPLDT and Smart partner with Capillary to unify loyalty programs\nOct 5, 2026\nNews\nPLDT Global executive urges culture-first leadership in Hong Kong business forum\nOct 2, 2026\nLATEST ARTICLES\nNews\nSubsea cables are critical infra requiring whole-of-nation protection – PLDT\nOct 14, 2026\nMalasakit (ESG)\nPLDT, Smart and Unilab Foundation bring crisis-tested learning program to more Philippine schools\nOct 13, 2026\nNews\nPLDT Global and Smart extend support to Filipinos in Saudi Arabia amid ongoing incident\nOct 13, 2026\nNews\nPLDT Group’s ERICA Wins 2026 AIBP Enterprise Innovation Award for Data and AI\nOct 9, 2026","domain":"main.pldt.com","id":2110626008217550848,"post_ts":1650470400000,"ss":[{"chunk_id":0,"content":"News Smart, regulators revisit vetoed SIM registration bill, push for global best practices for consumer protection Apr 21, 2022 Leading mobile services provider Smart Communications, Inc. (Smart) will bring to the table its expertise and knowledge on global best practices as it continues to work with government to ensure consumer protection through measures like the SIM card","ctx":{"span":[0,377]}},{"chunk_id":1,"content":"registration bill.","ctx":{"span":[0,17]}},{"chunk_id":2,"content":"registration bill. This comes after the President's recent veto of the measure and reports of the Senate President's announcement of his plan to use Congress' power to override the veto. \"Smart has long been in the forefront of consumer online protection and has been actively pushing programs toward this pursuit.","ctx":{"span":[0,313]}},{"chunk_id":3,"content":"This includes initiatives that keep our customers safe from scams and fraud, activities that uphold the highest standards of data privacy, and programs that promote safe online spaces for all, especially for children,\" said Alfredo S. Panlilio, PLDT Inc and Smart Communications President and CEO.","ctx":{"span":[0,296]}},{"chunk_id":4,"content":"\"More than supporting the legislative process, we at Smart are also willing to share our own experiences, as well as our knowledge on the best global practices, to contribute to the success of the SIM card registration bill, if and when it is passed into law.","ctx":{"span":[0,258]}},{"chunk_id":5,"content":"We also welcome any opportunity to support the government in developing the bill's implementing rules and regulations,\" Panlilio added. Speaking to reporters on the sidelines of PLDT's tower deal announcement, PLDT chair Manuel V. Pangilinan reiterated the company's support for the measure. \"We still are hoping that we will find a way to get the SIM cards registered.","ctx":{"span":[0,368]}},{"chunk_id":6,"content":"That's important, not only for our business, but for Filipinos in general.\" PLDT Chief Legal Counsel Marilyn V. Aquino also said: \"Before the veto, we were planning to work with regulators, and we were looking for best practices abroad, including rules and regulations that were adopted and how they were applied, including challenges encountered and mistakes that can be avoided.","ctx":{"span":[0,379]}},{"chunk_id":7,"content":"The plan is to work with regulators so that we can share information on what has happened as well as what is happening in other countries so that we don't make the same mistakes. That was the plan before the veto happened, and we will continue to do that.\" Smart and parent company PLDT have been active in collaborating with government and regulators for consumer protection.","ctx":{"span":[0,375]}},{"chunk_id":8,"content":"Through its Cybersecurity Operations Group, PLDT has invested billions to beef up its cybersecurity defenses, not only to protect its own infrastructure but mostly to help protect customers from cyberthreats and phishing and scamming activities.","ctx":{"span":[0,244]}},{"chunk_id":9,"content":"PLDT and Smart also regularly and actively campaign to inform and educate customers and help them identify red flags that indicate scams and fraud.","ctx":{"span":[0,146]}},{"chunk_id":10,"content":"PLDT and Smart have also embraced their role in the fight against online sexual abuse and exploitation of children (OSAEC) by rolling out relevant policies, technology solutions, and community programs that uphold the safety and welfare of children both online and offline.","ctx":{"span":[0,272]}},{"chunk_id":11,"content":"This includes investing in a pioneering Child Protection Platform and embedding it into the Group's 24/7 cyber security operations. This solution allows the Group to detect, predict, respond, and prevent domain and content-level access to child sexual abuse materials.","ctx":{"span":[0,267]}},{"chunk_id":12,"content":"As of end March 2022, PLDT and Smart have already blocked an accumulation of more than 1 billion user access attempts and over 224,000 online content and web pages linked to OSAEC. PLDT's Data Privacy Office has also been taking the lead in holding Group-wide data privacy trainings to equip leaders and employees alike as data privacy champions for customers.","ctx":{"span":[0,359]}},{"chunk_id":13,"content":"RELATED ARTICLES News Subsea cables are critical infra requiring whole-of-nation protection – PLDT Oct 14, 2026 News PLDT Global and Smart extend support to Filipinos in Saudi Arabia amid ongoing incident Oct 13, 2026 News PLDT Group’s ERICA Wins 2026 AIBP Enterprise Innovation Award for Data and AI Oct 9, 2026 News PLDT and Smart partner with Capillary to unify loyalty programs","ctx":{"span":[0,380]}},{"chunk_id":14,"content":"Oct 5, 2026 News PLDT Global executive urges culture-first leadership in Hong Kong business forum Oct 2, 2026 LATEST ARTICLES News Subsea cables are critical infra requiring whole-of-nation protection – PLDT Oct 14, 2026 Malasakit (ESG) PLDT, Smart and Unilab Foundation bring crisis-tested learning program to more Philippine schools Oct 13, 2026 News PLDT Global and Smart extend","ctx":{"span":[0,380]}},{"chunk_id":15,"content":"support to Filipinos in Saudi Arabia amid ongoing incident Oct 13, 2026 News PLDT Group’s ERICA Wins 2026 AIBP Enterprise Innovation Award for Data and AI Oct 9, 2026","ctx":{"span":[0,165]}}],"summary":"Official site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider","title":"Smart, regulators revisit vetoed SIM registration bill, push for global best practices for consumer protection","url":"https://main.pldt.com/article/smart-regulators-revisit-vetoed-sim-registration-bill-push-global-best-practices-consumer"},{"_indexCode":"PLDTRPAI_IDX_E15MHVUK","_indexName":"PLDT_data(PLDT_data)","_rank_index":4,"_rank_score":0.005627839,"_textrecall_index":4,"_textrecall_score":61.903748,"_x":{"a":1,"at":1792049592931,"au":"System","cts":1792043916899,"df":0,"op":1,"sbc":"PLDTRPAI_WEB_DLFTHNSX","srcId":2110611279277379584,"uts":1792049592931,"v":0},"content":"Malasakit (ESG)\nClaudia Barretto, Angelo Mendoza top-bill passion and purpose via PLDT, Smart’s Better Today\nMay 31, 2022\nPhotographer and filmmaker Angelo Mendoza shares how finding your passion becomes a powerful tool for self-reflection and self-love.\nPLDT and Smart invited artists, advocates, and mental health experts to share their stories anchored on Passion and Purpose, Strength and Resilience, Empathy and Community, and Hope. The storytelling initiative is PLDT and Smart’s second run of its Better Today Time Capsule Project, empowering the youth to find safe spaces to express themselves.\nWith the support of Canva Philippines, PLDT and Smart’s Better Today Time Capsule Project also encourages the youth to submit their own ‘time capsules’, which are works of art in the forms of music, spoken word, photography, and visual art.\nMental health advocate and musician Claudia Barretto shared her story on Passion and Purpose and how her music has become a form of catharsis and mental healthcare. She underscored the importance of becoming an authentic storyteller as a way to foster stronger relationships with other people.\nClaudia Barretto shares how her latest song “Be It” was inspired from her journaling.\n“It’s important to be honest about the story you’re trying to tell. The connection you build with other people is natural when you’re being truthful. [By] being an authentic storyteller, I can be vulnerable. I can speak my truth. I can tell my story,” Barretto shared.\nExpressing his own passion for art, photographer and filmmaker Angelo Mendoza shared how photography has enabled him to “find peace and joy in things that give us a sense of purpose”.\n“Finding your passion is a constant journey of self-reflection and self-love. It’s a difficult process, but it matters to try. The process [of photography] feels cathartic. I am able to cherish the present, and create a meaningful bond with the people and things I photograph by letting myself be a bit more vulnerable,” Mendoza said.\nBetter Today is a key part of PLDT and Smart’s continuing commitment to help the Philippines contribute to the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (UNSDG), particularly UNSDG #3 that stands for good health and well-being.\nThe top five winners of The Time Capsule Project will each receive PHP10,000 worth of connectivity from PLDT and Smart and a three-month premium subscription from Canva Philippines. They also have an opportunity to donate to their chosen mental health advocacy groups.\nRELATED ARTICLES\nMalasakit (ESG)\nPLDT, Smart and Unilab Foundation bring crisis-tested learning program to more Philippine schools\nOct 13, 2026\nMalasakit (ESG)\nBaguio deploys AI to improve ease-of-doing-business in Pine City\nOct 9, 2026\nMalasakit (ESG)\nA farmer’s journey towards digitalization\nOct 7, 2026\nMalasakit (ESG)\nMuntinlupa teachers put AI to work for more accessible and inclusive classrooms\nOct 5, 2026\nMalasakit (ESG)\nTacloban learners, educators champion safer, more resilient schools\nOct 2, 2026\nLATEST ARTICLES\nNews\nSubsea cables are critical infra requiring whole-of-nation protection – PLDT\nOct 14, 2026\nMalasakit (ESG)\nPLDT, Smart and Unilab Foundation bring crisis-tested learning program to more Philippine schools\nOct 13, 2026\nNews\nPLDT Global and Smart extend support to Filipinos in Saudi Arabia amid ongoing incident\nOct 13, 2026\nNews\nPLDT Group’s ERICA Wins 2026 AIBP Enterprise Innovation Award for Data and AI\nOct 9, 2026","domain":"main.pldt.com","id":2110626001892544512,"post_ts":1653926400000,"ss":[{"chunk_id":0,"content":"Malasakit (ESG)\nClaudia Barretto, Angelo Mendoza top-bill passion and purpose via PLDT, Smart’s Better Today\nMay 31, 2022\nPhotographer and filmmaker Angelo Mendoza shares how finding your passion becomes a powerful tool for self-reflection and self-love.","ctx":{"span":[0,253]}},{"chunk_id":1,"content":"PLDT and Smart invited artists, advocates, and mental health experts to share their stories anchored on Passion and Purpose, Strength and Resilience, Empathy and Community, and Hope. The storytelling initiative is PLDT and Smart’s second run of its Better Today Time Capsule Project, empowering the youth to find safe spaces to express themselves.","ctx":{"span":[0,346]}},{"chunk_id":2,"content":"With the support of Canva Philippines, PLDT and Smart’s Better Today Time Capsule Project also encourages the youth to submit their own ‘time capsules’, which are works of art in the forms of music, spoken word, photography, and visual art.","ctx":{"span":[0,239]}},{"chunk_id":3,"content":"Mental health advocate and musician Claudia Barretto shared her story on Passion and Purpose and how her music has become a form of catharsis and mental healthcare. She underscored the importance of becoming an authentic storyteller as a way to foster stronger relationships with other people. Claudia Barretto shares how her latest song “Be It” was inspired from her journaling.","ctx":{"span":[0,378]}},{"chunk_id":4,"content":"“It’s important to be honest about the story you’re trying to tell. The connection you build with other people is natural when you’re being truthful. [By] being an authentic storyteller, I can be vulnerable. I can speak my truth. I can tell my story,” Barretto shared.","ctx":{"span":[0,267]}},{"chunk_id":5,"content":"I can speak my truth. I can tell my story,” Barretto shared. Expressing his own passion for art, photographer and filmmaker Angelo Mendoza shared how photography has enabled him to “find peace and joy in things that give us a sense of purpose”. “Finding your passion is a constant journey of self-reflection and self-love. It’s a difficult process, but it matters to try.","ctx":{"span":[0,370]}},{"chunk_id":6,"content":"It’s a difficult process, but it matters to try. The process [of photography] feels cathartic. I am able to cherish the present, and create a meaningful bond with the people and things I photograph by letting myself be a bit more vulnerable,” Mendoza said.","ctx":{"span":[0,255]}},{"chunk_id":7,"content":"Better Today is a key part of PLDT and Smart’s continuing commitment to help the Philippines contribute to the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (UNSDG), particularly UNSDG #3 that stands for good health and well-being.","ctx":{"span":[0,229]}},{"chunk_id":8,"content":"The top five winners of The Time Capsule Project will each receive PHP10,000 worth of connectivity from PLDT and Smart and a three-month premium subscription from Canva Philippines. They also have an opportunity to donate to their chosen mental health advocacy groups.","ctx":{"span":[0,267]}},{"chunk_id":9,"content":"RELATED ARTICLES Malasakit (ESG) PLDT, Smart and Unilab Foundation bring crisis-tested learning program to more Philippine schools Oct 13, 2026 Malasakit (ESG) Baguio deploys AI to improve ease-of-doing-business in Pine City Oct 9, 2026 Malasakit (ESG) A farmer’s journey towards digitalization Oct 7, 2026 Malasakit (ESG) Muntinlupa teachers put AI to work for more accessible and","ctx":{"span":[0,380]}},{"chunk_id":10,"content":"inclusive classrooms Oct 5, 2026 Malasakit (ESG) Tacloban learners, educators champion safer, more resilient schools Oct 2, 2026 LATEST ARTICLES News Subsea cables are critical infra requiring whole-of-nation protection – PLDT Oct 14, 2026 Malasakit (ESG) PLDT, Smart and Unilab Foundation bring crisis-tested learning program to more Philippine schools Oct 13, 2026 News PLDT Global","ctx":{"span":[0,382]}},{"chunk_id":11,"content":"and Smart extend support to Filipinos in Saudi Arabia amid ongoing incident Oct 13, 2026 News PLDT Group’s ERICA Wins 2026 AIBP Enterprise Innovation Award for Data and AI Oct 9, 2026","ctx":{"span":[0,182]}}],"summary":"Official site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider","title":"Claudia Barretto, Angelo Mendoza top-bill passion and purpose via PLDT, Smart’s Better Today","url":"https://main.pldt.com/article/claudia-barretto-angelo-mendoza-top-bill-passion-and-purpose-pldt-smarts-better-today"},{"_indexCode":"PLDTRPAI_IDX_E15MHVUK","_indexName":"PLDT_data(PLDT_data)","_rank_index":5,"_rank_score":0.0053822263,"_semtrc_index":2,"_semtrc_score":0.0025684577,"_spanIds":[{"score":0.0025750676,"si":7,"text":"Invest in our planet, go paperless, say PLDT and Smart\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nLearn more about PLDT and Smart’s paperless billing program and how to access your bills by calling PLDT Home: 171; PLDT Enterprise: 177; Smart: *888. You may also visit www.pldtenterprise.com or www.pldthome.com. Smart customers may also log in to the GigaLife app for details.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0024413837,"si":2,"text":"Invest in our planet, go paperless, say PLDT and Smart\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\n“In addition to ensuring that our customers receive their bills faster and more securely, the migration to paperless billing supports the PLDT group’s overall sustainability efforts to use our planet’s resources more efficiently.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0023951,"si":1,"text":"Invest in our planet, go paperless, say PLDT and Smart\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nCustomers of PLDT Home, PLDT Enterprise, and Smart have been receiving electronic copies of their monthly statements following the migration to paperless billing.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0023861902,"si":4,"text":"Invest in our planet, go paperless, say PLDT and Smart\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nThe migration to digital billing helps save more than 9 million sheets of paper and about 93 liters of ink monthly from printing customers’ statements of account based on 2019 data. This translates to saving more than a thousand trees from being cut per month or around 12 hectares of forest annually.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0022974785,"si":0,"text":"Invest in our planet, go paperless, say PLDT and Smart\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nMalasakit (ESG)\nInvest in our planet, go paperless, say PLDT and Smart\nApr 28, 2022\nPLDT Inc. (PLDT) and Smart Communications, Inc. (Smart) are encouraging their customers to embrace the new digital billing program to join the global call for sustainable practices.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.002232664,"si":6,"text":"Invest in our planet, go paperless, say PLDT and Smart\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nThe PLDT group has recently released its decarbonization roadmap where it targets to reduce Scope 1 and 2 greenhouse gas emissions by 40% by year 2030. This paperless billing initiative supports the group’s commitment to help the country achieve the United Nations Sustainable Development Goal No. 12 on sustainable consumption and production.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0022064813,"si":8,"text":"Invest in our planet, go paperless, say PLDT and Smart\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nSmart customers may also log in to the GigaLife app for details. RELATED ARTICLES Malasakit (ESG) PLDT, Smart and Unilab Foundation bring crisis-tested learning program to more Philippine schools Oct 13, 2026 Malasakit (ESG) Baguio deploys AI to improve ease-of-doing-business in Pine City Oct 9, 2026 Malasakit (ESG) A farmer’s journey towards digitalization Oct 7, 2026 Malasakit","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0021202583,"si":10,"text":"Invest in our planet, go paperless, say PLDT and Smart\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nprogram to more Philippine schools Oct 13, 2026 News PLDT Global and Smart extend support to Filipinos in Saudi Arabia amid ongoing incident Oct 13, 2026 News PLDT Group’s ERICA Wins 2026 AIBP Enterprise Innovation Award for Data and AI Oct 9, 2026","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0021075422,"si":9,"text":"Invest in our planet, go paperless, say PLDT and Smart\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\n(ESG) Muntinlupa teachers put AI to work for more accessible and inclusive classrooms Oct 5, 2026 Malasakit (ESG) Tacloban learners, educators champion safer, more resilient schools Oct 2, 2026 LATEST ARTICLES News Subsea cables are critical infra requiring whole-of-nation protection – PLDT Oct 14, 2026 Malasakit (ESG) PLDT, Smart and Unilab Foundation bring crisis-tested learning","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0020647598,"si":5,"text":"Invest in our planet, go paperless, say PLDT and Smart\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nAs two of the country’s pioneers in sustainability, PLDT and Smart are the only telecommunication companies invited by the National Economic Development Authority (NEDA) to the Stakeholders’ Chamber on the Sustainable Development Goals. While the PLDT group continues to expand its infrastructure, it also invests in ecofriendly processes to lower its impact on the environment.","type":"semt"}],"_x":{"a":1,"at":1792049596702,"au":"System","cts":1792043917670,"df":0,"op":1,"sbc":"PLDTRPAI_WEB_DLFTHNSX","srcId":2110611282515382275,"uts":1792049596702,"v":0},"content":"Malasakit (ESG)\nInvest in our planet, go paperless, say PLDT and Smart\nApr 28, 2022\nPLDT Inc. (PLDT) and Smart Communications, Inc. (Smart) are encouraging their customers to embrace the new digital billing program to join the global call for sustainable practices. Customers of PLDT Home, PLDT Enterprise, and Smart have been receiving electronic copies of their monthly statements following the migration to paperless billing.\n“In addition to ensuring that our customers receive their bills faster and more securely, the migration to paperless billing supports the PLDT group’s overall sustainability efforts to use our planet’s resources more efficiently. As stewards of the environment, we align ourselves with like-minded organizations in the fight against climate change,” said Melissa Vergel De Dios, First Vice President and Chief Sustainability Officer at PLDT.\nThe migration to digital billing helps save more than 9 million sheets of paper and about 93 liters of ink monthly from printing customers’ statements of account based on 2019 data. This translates to saving more than a thousand trees from being cut per month or around 12 hectares of forest annually.\nAs two of the country’s pioneers in sustainability, PLDT and Smart are the only telecommunication companies invited by the National Economic Development Authority (NEDA) to the Stakeholders’ Chamber on the Sustainable Development Goals.\nWhile the PLDT group continues to expand its infrastructure, it also invests in ecofriendly processes to lower its impact on the environment. The PLDT group has recently released its decarbonization roadmap where it targets to reduce Scope 1 and 2 greenhouse gas emissions by 40% by year 2030.\nThis paperless billing initiative supports the group’s commitment to help the country achieve the United Nations Sustainable Development Goal No. 12 on sustainable consumption and production.\nLearn more about PLDT and Smart’s paperless billing program and how to access your bills by calling PLDT Home: 171; PLDT Enterprise: 177; Smart: *888. You may also visit www.pldtenterprise.com or www.pldthome.com. Smart customers may also log in to the GigaLife app for details.\nRELATED ARTICLES\nMalasakit (ESG)\nPLDT, Smart and Unilab Foundation bring crisis-tested learning program to more Philippine schools\nOct 13, 2026\nMalasakit (ESG)\nBaguio deploys AI to improve ease-of-doing-business in Pine City\nOct 9, 2026\nMalasakit (ESG)\nA farmer’s journey towards digitalization\nOct 7, 2026\nMalasakit (ESG)\nMuntinlupa teachers put AI to work for more accessible and inclusive classrooms\nOct 5, 2026\nMalasakit (ESG)\nTacloban learners, educators champion safer, more resilient schools\nOct 2, 2026\nLATEST ARTICLES\nNews\nSubsea cables are critical infra requiring whole-of-nation protection – PLDT\nOct 14, 2026\nMalasakit (ESG)\nPLDT, Smart and Unilab Foundation bring crisis-tested learning program to more Philippine schools\nOct 13, 2026\nNews\nPLDT Global and Smart extend support to Filipinos in Saudi Arabia amid ongoing incident\nOct 13, 2026\nNews\nPLDT Group’s ERICA Wins 2026 AIBP Enterprise Innovation Award for Data and AI\nOct 9, 2026","domain":"main.pldt.com","id":2110626005994569728,"post_ts":1651075200000,"ss":[{"chunk_id":0,"content":"Malasakit (ESG)\nInvest in our planet, go paperless, say PLDT and Smart\nApr 28, 2022\nPLDT Inc. (PLDT) and Smart Communications, Inc. (Smart) are encouraging their customers to embrace the new digital billing program to join the global call for sustainable practices.","ctx":{"span":[0,264]}},{"chunk_id":1,"content":"Customers of PLDT Home, PLDT Enterprise, and Smart have been receiving electronic copies of their monthly statements following the migration to paperless billing.","ctx":{"span":[0,161]}},{"chunk_id":2,"content":"“In addition to ensuring that our customers receive their bills faster and more securely, the migration to paperless billing supports the PLDT group’s overall sustainability efforts to use our planet’s resources more efficiently.","ctx":{"span":[0,228]}},{"chunk_id":3,"content":"As stewards of the environment, we align ourselves with like-minded organizations in the fight against climate change,” said Melissa Vergel De Dios, First Vice President and Chief Sustainability Officer at PLDT.","ctx":{"span":[0,210]}},{"chunk_id":4,"content":"The migration to digital billing helps save more than 9 million sheets of paper and about 93 liters of ink monthly from printing customers’ statements of account based on 2019 data. This translates to saving more than a thousand trees from being cut per month or around 12 hectares of forest annually.","ctx":{"span":[0,300]}},{"chunk_id":5,"content":"As two of the country’s pioneers in sustainability, PLDT and Smart are the only telecommunication companies invited by the National Economic Development Authority (NEDA) to the Stakeholders’ Chamber on the Sustainable Development Goals. While the PLDT group continues to expand its infrastructure, it also invests in ecofriendly processes to lower its impact on the environment.","ctx":{"span":[0,377]}},{"chunk_id":6,"content":"The PLDT group has recently released its decarbonization roadmap where it targets to reduce Scope 1 and 2 greenhouse gas emissions by 40% by year 2030. This paperless billing initiative supports the group’s commitment to help the country achieve the United Nations Sustainable Development Goal No. 12 on sustainable consumption and production.","ctx":{"span":[0,342]}},{"chunk_id":7,"content":"Learn more about PLDT and Smart’s paperless billing program and how to access your bills by calling PLDT Home: 171; PLDT Enterprise: 177; Smart: *888. You may also visit www.pldtenterprise.com or www.pldthome.com. Smart customers may also log in to the GigaLife app for details.","ctx":{"span":[0,277]}},{"chunk_id":8,"content":"Smart customers may also log in to the GigaLife app for details. RELATED ARTICLES Malasakit (ESG) PLDT, Smart and Unilab Foundation bring crisis-tested learning program to more Philippine schools Oct 13, 2026 Malasakit (ESG) Baguio deploys AI to improve ease-of-doing-business in Pine City Oct 9, 2026 Malasakit (ESG) A farmer’s journey towards digitalization Oct 7, 2026 Malasakit","ctx":{"span":[0,380]}},{"chunk_id":9,"content":"(ESG) Muntinlupa teachers put AI to work for more accessible and inclusive classrooms Oct 5, 2026 Malasakit (ESG) Tacloban learners, educators champion safer, more resilient schools Oct 2, 2026 LATEST ARTICLES News Subsea cables are critical infra requiring whole-of-nation protection – PLDT Oct 14, 2026 Malasakit (ESG) PLDT, Smart and Unilab Foundation bring crisis-tested learning","ctx":{"span":[0,382]}},{"chunk_id":10,"content":"program to more Philippine schools Oct 13, 2026 News PLDT Global and Smart extend support to Filipinos in Saudi Arabia amid ongoing incident Oct 13, 2026 News PLDT Group’s ERICA Wins 2026 AIBP Enterprise Innovation Award for Data and AI Oct 9, 2026","ctx":{"span":[0,247]}}],"summary":"Official site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider","title":"Invest in our planet, go paperless, say PLDT and Smart","url":"https://main.pldt.com/article/invest-our-planet-go-paperless-say-pldt-and-smart"},{"_indexCode":"PLDTRPAI_IDX_E15MHVUK","_indexName":"PLDT_data(PLDT_data)","_rank_index":6,"_rank_score":0.0029105213,"_semtrc_index":9,"_semtrc_score":0.002479523,"_spanIds":[{"score":0.002494152,"si":8,"text":"PLDT and Smart offer 6-month installment bills payments\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nWe encourage you to pay the amount due in full to ensure continuous service. RELATED ARTICLES Advisories PLDT cable cut advisory Oct. 2, 2026 Oct 2, 2026 Advisories PLDT, Smart Inday, habagat advisory Jul 8, 2026 Advisories PLDT, Smart Mindanao earthquake advisory Jun 9, 2026 Advisories PLDT, Smart ‘Mayon’ advisory May 6, 2026 Advisories PLDT, Smart #UwanPH Advisory Nov 8, 2025","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0024310383,"si":7,"text":"PLDT and Smart offer 6-month installment bills payments\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nI cannot pay the total amount for the installment period. Will my internet service get restricted? Payments received less than the amount due may result to the temporary restriction of your internet service. We encourage you to pay the amount due in full to ensure continuous service.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0023913267,"si":1,"text":"PLDT and Smart offer 6-month installment bills payments\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nUnder this payment program, PLDT Home customers, and, Smart and Sun consumer postpaid subscribers can settle their unpaid balances as of April 30 in six equal monthly payments with 0% interest and no penalties. “We hope that through this payment program, we will help keep you connected whether you are at home, the office or elsewhere after the enhanced community quarantine period.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0023867614,"si":2,"text":"PLDT and Smart offer 6-month installment bills payments\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nAs one community, we will get through these challenging times together,” said Manuel V. Pangilinan, PLDT Inc. Chairman and CEO. FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS\nHow can I track my charges? You can track your bills and payments through the MyPLDT-Smart App. If the payment extension is over, will I have to pay for 2 months?","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0023727112,"si":3,"text":"PLDT and Smart offer 6-month installment bills payments\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nIf the payment extension is over, will I have to pay for 2 months? After the payment extension, we will send you your bill reflecting the first installment amount due. This will cover all outstanding balance as of April 30, 2020, equally divided in 6 months with no added interest or penalties for late payment. I missed payment in one of the installment periods.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0023659903,"si":5,"text":"PLDT and Smart offer 6-month installment bills payments\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nNo, you do not need to enroll. All postpaid PLDT Home accounts are eligible for the 6 months installment program with no interest and late payment charges. I do not want to avail of the deferred payment scheme. Can I pay my bills in full? Yes, you may pay your outstanding balance in full. You may pay in any of our online payment channels at home.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0023581202,"si":6,"text":"PLDT and Smart offer 6-month installment bills payments\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nYou may pay in any of our online payment channels at home. I want to complete paying my bill for a shorter period. Do you have other installment schemes? All postpaid accounts will be automatically enrolled for the 6 months installment scheme. If you wish to complete payment earlier, you may pay more than the amount due for the month.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.002324453,"si":0,"text":"PLDT and Smart offer 6-month installment bills payments\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nAdvisories\nPLDT and Smart offer 6-month installment bills payments\nApr 15, 2020\nTo help ease the financial burden of its customers during the COVID crisis, PLDT Inc. and Smart Communications will start implementing on May 1 a 6-month installment payment program for the outstanding monthly bills of its postpaid subscribers.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0023222335,"si":4,"text":"PLDT and Smart offer 6-month installment bills payments\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nI missed payment in one of the installment periods. What happens to my account? Missed payments in any of the installment periods will go through the normal collection process. We encourage you to settle your bill in full on or before the due date to ensure continuous service. Do I need to enroll to avail of deferred payment? No, you do not need to enroll.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0022078701,"si":9,"text":"PLDT and Smart offer 6-month installment bills payments\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nLATEST ARTICLES News Subsea cables are critical infra requiring whole-of-nation protection – PLDT Oct 14, 2026 Malasakit (ESG) PLDT, Smart and Unilab Foundation bring crisis-tested learning program to more Philippine schools Oct 13, 2026 News PLDT Global and Smart extend support to Filipinos in Saudi Arabia amid ongoing incident Oct 13, 2026 News PLDT Group’s ERICA Wins 2026 AIBP","type":"semt"}],"_x":{"a":1,"at":1792049596705,"au":"System","cts":1792043917652,"df":0,"op":1,"sbc":"PLDTRPAI_WEB_DLFTHNSX","srcId":2110611282439884802,"uts":1792049596705,"v":0},"content":"Advisories\nPLDT and Smart offer 6-month installment bills payments\nApr 15, 2020\nTo help ease the financial burden of its customers during the COVID crisis, PLDT Inc. and Smart Communications will start implementing on May 1 a 6-month installment payment program for the outstanding monthly bills of its postpaid subscribers.\nUnder this payment program, PLDT Home customers, and, Smart and Sun consumer postpaid subscribers can settle their unpaid balances as of April 30 in six equal monthly payments with 0% interest and no penalties.\n“We hope that through this payment program, we will help keep you connected whether you are at home, the office or elsewhere after the enhanced community quarantine period. As one community, we will get through these challenging times together,” said Manuel V. Pangilinan, PLDT Inc. Chairman and CEO.\nFREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS\nHow can I track my charges?\nYou can track your bills and payments through the MyPLDT-Smart App.\nIf the payment extension is over, will I have to pay for 2 months?\nAfter the payment extension, we will send you your bill reflecting the first installment amount due. This will cover all outstanding balance as of April 30, 2020, equally divided in 6 months with no added interest or penalties for late payment.\nI missed payment in one of the installment periods. What happens to my account?\nMissed payments in any of the installment periods will go through the normal collection process. We encourage you to settle your bill in full on or before the due date to ensure continuous service.\nDo I need to enroll to avail of deferred payment?\nNo, you do not need to enroll. All postpaid PLDT Home accounts are eligible for the 6 months installment program with no interest and late payment charges.\nI do not want to avail of the deferred payment scheme. Can I pay my bills in full?\nYes, you may pay your outstanding balance in full. You may pay in any of our online payment channels at home.\nI want to complete paying my bill for a shorter period. Do you have other installment schemes?\nAll postpaid accounts will be automatically enrolled for the 6 months installment scheme. If you wish to complete payment earlier, you may pay more than the amount due for the month.\nI cannot pay the total amount for the installment period. Will my internet service get restricted?\nPayments received less than the amount due may result to the temporary restriction of your internet service. We encourage you to pay the amount due in full to ensure continuous service.\nRELATED ARTICLES\nAdvisories\nPLDT cable cut advisory Oct. 2, 2026\nOct 2, 2026\nAdvisories\nPLDT, Smart Inday, habagat advisory\nJul 8, 2026\nAdvisories\nPLDT, Smart Mindanao earthquake advisory\nJun 9, 2026\nAdvisories\nPLDT, Smart ‘Mayon’ advisory\nMay 6, 2026\nAdvisories\nPLDT, Smart #UwanPH Advisory\nNov 8, 2025\nLATEST ARTICLES\nNews\nSubsea cables are critical infra requiring whole-of-nation protection – PLDT\nOct 14, 2026\nMalasakit (ESG)\nPLDT, Smart and Unilab Foundation bring crisis-tested learning program to more Philippine schools\nOct 13, 2026\nNews\nPLDT Global and Smart extend support to Filipinos in Saudi Arabia amid ongoing incident\nOct 13, 2026\nNews\nPLDT Group’s ERICA Wins 2026 AIBP Enterprise Innovation Award for Data and AI\nOct 9, 2026","domain":"main.pldt.com","id":2110626002840453120,"post_ts":1586880000000,"ss":[{"chunk_id":0,"content":"Advisories\nPLDT and Smart offer 6-month installment bills payments\nApr 15, 2020\nTo help ease the financial burden of its customers during the COVID crisis, PLDT Inc. and Smart Communications will start implementing on May 1 a 6-month installment payment program for the outstanding monthly bills of its postpaid subscribers.","ctx":{"span":[0,323]}},{"chunk_id":1,"content":"Under this payment program, PLDT Home customers, and, Smart and Sun consumer postpaid subscribers can settle their unpaid balances as of April 30 in six equal monthly payments with 0% interest and no penalties. “We hope that through this payment program, we will help keep you connected whether you are at home, the office or elsewhere after the enhanced community quarantine period.","ctx":{"span":[0,382]}},{"chunk_id":2,"content":"As one community, we will get through these challenging times together,” said Manuel V. Pangilinan, PLDT Inc. Chairman and CEO. FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS\nHow can I track my charges? You can track your bills and payments through the MyPLDT-Smart App. If the payment extension is over, will I have to pay for 2 months?","ctx":{"span":[0,316]}},{"chunk_id":3,"content":"If the payment extension is over, will I have to pay for 2 months? After the payment extension, we will send you your bill reflecting the first installment amount due. This will cover all outstanding balance as of April 30, 2020, equally divided in 6 months with no added interest or penalties for late payment. I missed payment in one of the installment periods.","ctx":{"span":[0,362]}},{"chunk_id":4,"content":"I missed payment in one of the installment periods. What happens to my account? Missed payments in any of the installment periods will go through the normal collection process. We encourage you to settle your bill in full on or before the due date to ensure continuous service. Do I need to enroll to avail of deferred payment? No, you do not need to enroll.","ctx":{"span":[0,357]}},{"chunk_id":5,"content":"No, you do not need to enroll. All postpaid PLDT Home accounts are eligible for the 6 months installment program with no interest and late payment charges. I do not want to avail of the deferred payment scheme. Can I pay my bills in full? Yes, you may pay your outstanding balance in full. You may pay in any of our online payment channels at home.","ctx":{"span":[0,347]}},{"chunk_id":6,"content":"You may pay in any of our online payment channels at home. I want to complete paying my bill for a shorter period. Do you have other installment schemes? All postpaid accounts will be automatically enrolled for the 6 months installment scheme. If you wish to complete payment earlier, you may pay more than the amount due for the month.","ctx":{"span":[0,335]}},{"chunk_id":7,"content":"I cannot pay the total amount for the installment period. Will my internet service get restricted? Payments received less than the amount due may result to the temporary restriction of your internet service. We encourage you to pay the amount due in full to ensure continuous service.","ctx":{"span":[0,283]}},{"chunk_id":8,"content":"We encourage you to pay the amount due in full to ensure continuous service. RELATED ARTICLES Advisories PLDT cable cut advisory Oct. 2, 2026 Oct 2, 2026 Advisories PLDT, Smart Inday, habagat advisory Jul 8, 2026 Advisories PLDT, Smart Mindanao earthquake advisory Jun 9, 2026 Advisories PLDT, Smart ‘Mayon’ advisory May 6, 2026 Advisories PLDT, Smart #UwanPH Advisory Nov 8, 2025","ctx":{"span":[0,379]}},{"chunk_id":9,"content":"LATEST ARTICLES News Subsea cables are critical infra requiring whole-of-nation protection – PLDT Oct 14, 2026 Malasakit (ESG) PLDT, Smart and Unilab Foundation bring crisis-tested learning program to more Philippine schools Oct 13, 2026 News PLDT Global and Smart extend support to Filipinos in Saudi Arabia amid ongoing incident Oct 13, 2026 News PLDT Group’s ERICA Wins 2026 AIBP","ctx":{"span":[0,381]}},{"chunk_id":10,"content":"Enterprise Innovation Award for Data and AI Oct 9, 2026","ctx":{"span":[0,54]}}],"summary":"Official site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider","title":"PLDT and Smart offer 6-month installment bills payments","url":"https://main.pldt.com/article/pldt-and-smart-offer-6-month-installment-bills-payments"},{"_indexCode":"PLDTRPAI_IDX_E15MHVUK","_indexName":"PLDT_data(PLDT_data)","_rank_index":7,"_rank_score":0.0026693766,"_semtrc_index":18,"_semtrc_score":0.002442787,"_spanIds":[{"score":0.0025496294,"si":5,"text":"PLDT, Smart support Department of Finance pilot on e-invoicing, expand digital billing\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nThis complements the paperless billing program we are implementing for our Enterprise customers,” said Attorney Ma. Criselda Guhit, First Vice President of PLDT’s Tax Management and Advocacy Sector. Starting April, Enterprise customers of PLDT and Smart may be able to view their statements of account through online channels, as the PLDT group shifts to paperless billing.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.002474541,"si":7,"text":"PLDT, Smart support Department of Finance pilot on e-invoicing, expand digital billing\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nIt also reinforces the Group's commitment to help the country achieve the United Nations Sustainable Development Goal No. 12 on sustainable consumption and production. Learn more about PLDT and Smart’s paperless billing program and how to access your bills by calling PLDT Home: 171; PLDT Enterprise: 177; Smart: *888; Smart Enterprise: #888.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0023806128,"si":6,"text":"PLDT, Smart support Department of Finance pilot on e-invoicing, expand digital billing\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nThis bolsters the earlier implementation of the same arrangement for the group’s wireless subscribers and home broadband customers. The digital billing program is aligned with the PLDT group’s aim to improve customer experience by ensuring timely and accurate billing and to protect data privacy, and to streamline processes in its group-wide pivot to digital transformation.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0023436625,"si":9,"text":"PLDT, Smart support Department of Finance pilot on e-invoicing, expand digital billing\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nSmart customers may also log in to the GigaLife app for details. RELATED ARTICLES News Subsea cables are critical infra requiring whole-of-nation protection – PLDT Oct 14, 2026 News PLDT Global and Smart extend support to Filipinos in Saudi Arabia amid ongoing incident Oct 13, 2026 News PLDT Group’s ERICA Wins 2026 AIBP Enterprise Innovation Award for Data and AI Oct 9, 2026 News","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0023095377,"si":2,"text":"PLDT, Smart support Department of Finance pilot on e-invoicing, expand digital billing\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nUnder the TRAIN law, taxpayers engaged in the export of goods or services, e-commerce and those considered large taxpayers, are required to issue e-invoices or e-receipts for their transactions within five years from the law’s effectivity, or on or before January 1, 2023.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0023035004,"si":4,"text":"PLDT, Smart support Department of Finance pilot on e-invoicing, expand digital billing\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\n“The PLDT group supports the government’s efforts to improve the country’s tax collection and administration. As responsible corporate citizens helping drive the government’s digitalization, we piloted the issuance of e-invoices and e-receipts, in fulfillment of our mandate under the law.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0022902272,"si":0,"text":"PLDT, Smart support Department of Finance pilot on e-invoicing, expand digital billing\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nNews\nPLDT, Smart support Department of Finance pilot on e-invoicing, expand digital billing\nMar 24, 2022\nPLDT and Smart Communications, Inc. support the push of the Department of Finance for the mandatory issuance of electronic invoicing system (EIS), supporting the Group’s Enterprise customers covered by the expanded digital or paperless billing program.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0022884163,"si":8,"text":"PLDT, Smart support Department of Finance pilot on e-invoicing, expand digital billing\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nYou may also visit www.pldtenterprise.com or www.pldthome.com. Smart customers may also log in to the GigaLife app for details.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0022807994,"si":3,"text":"PLDT, Smart support Department of Finance pilot on e-invoicing, expand digital billing\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nAhead of the mandatory implementation next year, PLDT and Smart, classified as large taxpayers by the Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR), were chosen to take part in the pilot implementation of the EIS. By July 2022, BIR requires the country’s 100 large taxpayers to launch e-invoicing.","type":"semt"},{"score":0.0022561764,"si":11,"text":"PLDT, Smart support Department of Finance pilot on e-invoicing, expand digital billing\nOfficial site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider\nPhilippine schools Oct 13, 2026 News PLDT Global and Smart extend support to Filipinos in Saudi Arabia amid ongoing incident Oct 13, 2026 News PLDT Group’s ERICA Wins 2026 AIBP Enterprise Innovation Award for Data and AI Oct 9, 2026","type":"semt"}],"_x":{"a":1,"at":1792049621718,"au":"System","cts":1792043917131,"df":0,"op":1,"sbc":"PLDTRPAI_WEB_DLFTHNSX","srcId":2110611280254652417,"uts":1792049621718,"v":0},"content":"News\nPLDT, Smart support Department of Finance pilot on e-invoicing, expand digital billing\nMar 24, 2022\nPLDT and Smart Communications, Inc. support the push of the Department of Finance for the mandatory issuance of electronic invoicing system (EIS), supporting the Group’s Enterprise customers covered by the expanded digital or paperless billing program.\nTo reduce Value Added Tax (VAT) tax fraud and simplify transactions for taxpayers, electronic invoice (e-invoice) or electronic receipt (e-receipt) issuance became mandatory in the Philippines when the Tax Reform for Acceleration and Inclusion Act (TRAIN) law took effect in 2018.\nUnder the TRAIN law, taxpayers engaged in the export of goods or services, e-commerce and those considered large taxpayers, are required to issue e-invoices or e-receipts for their transactions within five years from the law’s effectivity, or on or before January 1, 2023.\nAhead of the mandatory implementation next year, PLDT and Smart, classified as large taxpayers by the Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR), were chosen to take part in the pilot implementation of the EIS. By July 2022, BIR requires the country’s 100 large taxpayers to launch e-invoicing.\n“The PLDT group supports the government’s efforts to improve the country’s tax collection and administration. As responsible corporate citizens helping drive the government’s digitalization, we piloted the issuance of e-invoices and e-receipts, in fulfillment of our mandate under the law. This complements the paperless billing program we are implementing for our Enterprise customers,” said Attorney Ma. Criselda Guhit, First Vice President of PLDT’s Tax Management and Advocacy Sector.\nStarting April, Enterprise customers of PLDT and Smart may be able to view their statements of account through online channels, as the PLDT group shifts to paperless billing. This bolsters the earlier implementation of the same arrangement for the group’s wireless subscribers and home broadband customers.\nThe digital billing program is aligned with the PLDT group’s aim to improve customer experience by ensuring timely and accurate billing and to protect data privacy, and to streamline processes in its group-wide pivot to digital transformation. It also reinforces the Group's commitment to help the country achieve the United Nations Sustainable Development Goal No. 12 on sustainable consumption and production.\nLearn more about PLDT and Smart’s paperless billing program and how to access your bills by calling PLDT Home: 171; PLDT Enterprise: 177; Smart: *888; Smart Enterprise: #888. You may also visit www.pldtenterprise.com or www.pldthome.com. Smart customers may also log in to the GigaLife app for details.\nRELATED ARTICLES\nNews\nSubsea cables are critical infra requiring whole-of-nation protection – PLDT\nOct 14, 2026\nNews\nPLDT Global and Smart extend support to Filipinos in Saudi Arabia amid ongoing incident\nOct 13, 2026\nNews\nPLDT Group’s ERICA Wins 2026 AIBP Enterprise Innovation Award for Data and AI\nOct 9, 2026\nNews\nPLDT and Smart partner with Capillary to unify loyalty programs\nOct 5, 2026\nNews\nPLDT Global executive urges culture-first leadership in Hong Kong business forum\nOct 2, 2026\nLATEST ARTICLES\nNews\nSubsea cables are critical infra requiring whole-of-nation protection – PLDT\nOct 14, 2026\nMalasakit (ESG)\nPLDT, Smart and Unilab Foundation bring crisis-tested learning program to more Philippine schools\nOct 13, 2026\nNews\nPLDT Global and Smart extend support to Filipinos in Saudi Arabia amid ongoing incident\nOct 13, 2026\nNews\nPLDT Group’s ERICA Wins 2026 AIBP Enterprise Innovation Award for Data and AI\nOct 9, 2026","domain":"main.pldt.com","id":2110626008850894848,"post_ts":1648051200000,"ss":[{"chunk_id":0,"content":"News\nPLDT, Smart support Department of Finance pilo