line channels, as the PLDT group shifts to paperless billing.","ctx":{"span":[0,372]}},{"chunk_id":6,"content":"This bolsters the earlier implementation of the same arrangement for the group’s wireless subscribers and home broadband customers. The digital billing program is aligned with the PLDT group’s aim to improve customer experience by ensuring timely and accurate billing and to protect data privacy, and to streamline processes in its group-wide pivot to digital transformation.","ctx":{"span":[0,374]}},{"chunk_id":7,"content":"It also reinforces the Group's commitment to help the country achieve the United Nations Sustainable Development Goal No. 12 on sustainable consumption and production. Learn more about PLDT and Smart’s paperless billing program and how to access your bills by calling PLDT Home: 171; PLDT Enterprise: 177; Smart: *888; Smart Enterprise: #888.","ctx":{"span":[0,341]}},{"chunk_id":8,"content":"You may also visit www.pldtenterprise.com or www.pldthome.com. Smart customers may also log in to the GigaLife app for details.","ctx":{"span":[0,126]}},{"chunk_id":9,"content":"Smart customers may also log in to the GigaLife app for details. RELATED ARTICLES News Subsea cables are critical infra requiring whole-of-nation protection – PLDT Oct 14, 2026 News PLDT Global and Smart extend support to Filipinos in Saudi Arabia amid ongoing incident Oct 13, 2026 News PLDT Group’s ERICA Wins 2026 AIBP Enterprise Innovation Award for Data and AI Oct 9, 2026 News","ctx":{"span":[0,381]}},{"chunk_id":10,"content":"PLDT and Smart partner with Capillary to unify loyalty programs Oct 5, 2026 News PLDT Global executive urges culture-first leadership in Hong Kong business forum Oct 2, 2026 LATEST ARTICLES News Subsea cables are critical infra requiring whole-of-nation protection – PLDT Oct 14, 2026 Malasakit (ESG) PLDT, Smart and Unilab Foundation bring crisis-tested learning program to more","ctx":{"span":[0,378]}},{"chunk_id":11,"content":"Philippine schools Oct 13, 2026 News PLDT Global and Smart extend support to Filipinos in Saudi Arabia amid ongoing incident Oct 13, 2026 News PLDT Group’s ERICA Wins 2026 AIBP Enterprise Innovation Award for Data and AI Oct 9, 2026","ctx":{"span":[0,231]}}],"summary":"Official site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider","title":"PLDT, Smart support Department of Finance pilot on e-invoicing, expand digital billing","url":"https://main.pldt.com/article/pldt-smart-support-department-finance-pilot-e-invoicing-expand-digital-billing"},{"_indexCode":"PLDTRPAI_IDX_E15MHVUK","_indexName":"PLDT_data(PLDT_data)","_rank_index":8,"_rank_score":0.0024790484,"_textrecall_index":2,"_textrecall_score":70.30504,"_x":{"a":1,"at":1792049596205,"au":"System","cts":1792043917439,"df":0,"op":1,"sbc":"PLDTRPAI_WEB_DLFTHNSX","srcId":2110611281546498052,"uts":1792049596205,"v":0},"content":"Malasakit (ESG)\nPLDT, Smart provide bill reprieve, free calls, relief good to quake victims\nJul 30, 2022\nEfforts of PLDT, Smart Communications, Inc. (Smart) and PLDT-Smart Foundation (PSF) are still underway to provide immediate assistance in the form of communication as aid, relief goods, and hygiene kits to communities affected by the recent Magnitude 7 earthquake that rocked North Luzon.\nCommunication as aid\nTo help residents get back on their feet, PLDT and Smart have assured impacted customers of continued service, with the deferment of disconnection for non-payment of PLDT Home and Smart postpaid bills, until August 15. Smart has also provided emergency load assistance to customers in the quake-hit areas of Abra, Benguet, Ilocos Sur and Mountain Province.\nPLDT and Smart have also reopened their stores to serve the public. Stores in Bangued, Bucay, Dolores, Lagangilang, Penarrubia, San Juan and Tayum in Abra; La Trinidad in Benguet; Bantay, Candon, and Vigan in Ilocos Sur; Bauko, Sadanga, Sagada and Tadian in Mountain Province, are now available to cater to the needs of PLDT and Smart customers.\nFree calls and wifi services continue\nLibreng Tawag and Libreng Wi-Fi stations continue to provide much needed connectivity to affected communities, allowing them to communicate with their families and loved ones. The following stations will continue to operate until August 3:\nAbra\nTown Plaza. Bangued, Abra\nIlocos Sur\nLandmark Bldg, Jose Singson St, Poblacion, Vigan City, Ilocos Sur\nMore help on the way\nVolunteers and partners of PLDT, Smart, and PSF are also working round the clock to prepare relief goods for turnover to the Provincial Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council (PDRRMC) to benefit hardest hit communities in the coming days.\nFor more information on the earthquake response efforts of PLDT and Smart, visit: https://bit.ly/PLDTSmartLuzonEarthquakeAdvisory.\nRELATED ARTICLES\nMalasakit (ESG)\nPLDT, Smart and Unilab Foundation bring crisis-tested learning program to more Philippine schools\nOct 13, 2026\nMalasakit (ESG)\nBaguio deploys AI to improve ease-of-doing-business in Pine City\nOct 9, 2026\nMalasakit (ESG)\nA farmer’s journey towards digitalization\nOct 7, 2026\nMalasakit (ESG)\nMuntinlupa teachers put AI to work for more accessible and inclusive classrooms\nOct 5, 2026\nMalasakit (ESG)\nTacloban learners, educators champion safer, more resilient schools\nOct 2, 2026\nLATEST ARTICLES\nNews\nSubsea cables are critical infra requiring whole-of-nation protection – PLDT\nOct 14, 2026\nMalasakit (ESG)\nPLDT, Smart and Unilab Foundation bring crisis-tested learning program to more Philippine schools\nOct 13, 2026\nNews\nPLDT Global and Smart extend support to Filipinos in Saudi Arabia amid ongoing incident\nOct 13, 2026\nNews\nPLDT Group’s ERICA Wins 2026 AIBP Enterprise Innovation Award for Data and AI\nOct 9, 2026","domain":"main.pldt.com","id":2110626007861035008,"post_ts":1659110400000,"ss":[{"chunk_id":0,"content":"Malasakit (ESG) PLDT, Smart provide bill reprieve, free calls, relief good to quake victims Jul 30, 2022 Efforts of PLDT, Smart Communications, Inc. (Smart) and PLDT-Smart Foundation (PSF) are still underway to provide immediate assistance in the form of communication as aid, relief goods, and hygiene kits to communities affected by the recent Magnitude 7 earthquake that rocked","ctx":{"span":[0,379]}},{"chunk_id":1,"content":"North Luzon.","ctx":{"span":[0,11]}},{"chunk_id":2,"content":"North Luzon. Communication as aid\nTo help residents get back on their feet, PLDT and Smart have assured impacted customers of continued service, with the deferment of disconnection for non-payment of PLDT Home and Smart postpaid bills, until August 15.","ctx":{"span":[0,251]}},{"chunk_id":3,"content":"Smart has also provided emergency load assistance to customers in the quake-hit areas of Abra, Benguet, Ilocos Sur and Mountain Province. PLDT and Smart have also reopened their stores to serve the public.","ctx":{"span":[0,204]}},{"chunk_id":4,"content":"PLDT and Smart have also reopened their stores to serve the public. Stores in Bangued, Bucay, Dolores, Lagangilang, Penarrubia, San Juan and Tayum in Abra; La Trinidad in Benguet; Bantay, Candon, and Vigan in Ilocos Sur; Bauko, Sadanga, Sagada and Tadian in Mountain Province, are now available to cater to the needs of PLDT and Smart customers.","ctx":{"span":[0,344]}},{"chunk_id":5,"content":"Free calls and wifi services continue\nLibreng Tawag and Libreng Wi-Fi stations continue to provide much needed connectivity to affected communities, allowing them to communicate with their families and loved ones. The following stations will continue to operate until August 3:\nAbra\nTown Plaza.","ctx":{"span":[0,293]}},{"chunk_id":6,"content":"Bangued, Abra\nIlocos Sur\nLandmark Bldg, Jose Singson St, Poblacion, Vigan City, Ilocos Sur\nMore help on the way\nVolunteers and partners of PLDT, Smart, and PSF are also working round the clock to prepare relief goods for turnover to the Provincial Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council (PDRRMC) to benefit hardest hit communities in the coming days.","ctx":{"span":[0,357]}},{"chunk_id":7,"content":"For more information on the earthquake response efforts of PLDT and Smart, visit: https://bit.ly/PLDTSmartLuzonEarthquakeAdvisory.","ctx":{"span":[0,129]}},{"chunk_id":8,"content":"RELATED ARTICLES Malasakit (ESG) PLDT, Smart and Unilab Foundation bring crisis-tested learning program to more Philippine schools Oct 13, 2026 Malasakit (ESG) Baguio deploys AI to improve ease-of-doing-business in Pine City Oct 9, 2026 Malasakit (ESG) A farmer’s journey towards digitalization Oct 7, 2026 Malasakit (ESG) Muntinlupa teachers put AI to work for more accessible and","ctx":{"span":[0,380]}},{"chunk_id":9,"content":"inclusive classrooms Oct 5, 2026 Malasakit (ESG) Tacloban learners, educators champion safer, more resilient schools Oct 2, 2026 LATEST ARTICLES News Subsea cables are critical infra requiring whole-of-nation protection – PLDT Oct 14, 2026 Malasakit (ESG) PLDT, Smart and Unilab Foundation bring crisis-tested learning program to more Philippine schools Oct 13, 2026 News PLDT Global","ctx":{"span":[0,382]}},{"chunk_id":10,"content":"and Smart extend support to Filipinos in Saudi Arabia amid ongoing incident Oct 13, 2026 News PLDT Group’s ERICA Wins 2026 AIBP Enterprise Innovation Award for Data and AI Oct 9, 2026","ctx":{"span":[0,182]}}],"summary":"Official site of the Philippines' leading telecommunications and digital services provider","title":"PLDT, Smart provide bill reprieve, free calls, relief good to quake victims","url":"https://main.pldt.com/article/pldt-smart-provide-bill-reprieve-free-calls-relief-good-quake-victims"},{"_indexCode":"PLDTRPAI_IDX_E15MHVUK","_indexName":"PLDT_data(PLDT_data)","_rank_index":9,"_rank_score":0.0018719345,"_textrecall_index":3,"_textrecall_score":68.49105,"_x":{"a":1,"at":1792049593434,"au":"System","cts":1792043917149,"df":0,"op":1,"sbc":"PLDTRPAI_WEB_DLFTHNSX","srcId":2110611280330149891,"uts":1792049593434,"v":0},"content":"Innovation\nDynamic learning, cybersecurity top bill PLDT, Smart innovations for school year\nOct 7, 2021\nPLDT and wireless unit Smart Communications, Inc. are boosting e-learning in the new school year with two new courses on the Innovations Academy for Disaster Awareness, Preparedness, and Training (iADAPT) platform.\nPowered by the Philippine Disaster Resilience Foundation, iADAPT houses interactive courses developed by industry leaders on risk reduction and management, business continuity, and climate change adaptation. This school year, two new e-learning courses, the CyberSmart and the Central Visayan Institute Foundation-Dynamic Learning Program (CVIF-DLP) will be made available to Smart partner schools and the Department of Education (DepEd) divisions on the iADAPT platform. The first 300 registrants on the site will be able to access the courses for free.\n“The new school year presents new challenges for students and teachers as they continue education through blended learning. Smart offers innovative programs that ensure no learner is left behind and protect Filipinos against online threats as they rely on the internet for school and work,” said Stephanie V. Orlino, Smart Assistant Vice President and Head of Community Relations.\nLearn Smart and Work Smart at home\nCentered around the CyberSmart Investigation Agency, the cybersecurity course includes topics on online child safety, data privacy and security, gadget protection, spotting and combating fake news, and responsible use of social media, as well as digital wellbeing and mental health.\nCyberSmart is a collaboration between various business units across PLDT and Smart. It is supported by the DepEd, the National Privacy Commission, UNICEF, International Justice Mission, and Internet Watch Foundation..\nPandemic-resilient education program\nAccredited by the DepEd as a supplementary resource, the CVIF-DLP works well with blended learning whether students are at home or in a limited face-to-face setting. The program develops them into independent learners through the self-directed CVIF-DLP Learning Activity Sheets (CVIF-DLP LAS).\nPLDT, Smart, and the PLDT-Smart Foundation have backed the crisis-resilient teaching method developed by renowned Filipino Theoretical Physicists and Ramon Magsaysay Awardees for Education Dr. Christopher Bernido and Dr. Ma. Victoria Carpio-Bernido since 2010.\nSo far, Smart has trained over 13,800 teachers in 753 public and private schools and five alternative learning system divisions and helped produce 2,235 CVIF-DLP LAS free to download at the DepEd Commons.\nPLDT and Smart foster learning through technology to help the nation achieve the United Nation’s Sustainable Development Goal (SDG) #4: Quality Education.\nCheck out PLDT and Smart learning materials at https://iadapt.pdrf.org/SMART.\nRELATED ARTICLES\nInnovation\nPLDT and Smart support United Nations-led ethical AI agenda\nDec 20, 2023\nInnovation\nPLDT Breaks Ground for 11th and Largest Hyperscale Data Center\nMar 18, 2022\nInnovation\nJ.A.R.V.I.S.-like program for business wins PLDT, Smart startup tilt\nNov 22, 2021\nInnovation\nPLDT champions startups, widens search for innovations\nNov 18, 2021\nInnovation\nPLDT, Smart outpace competition in fiber, mobile, fixed wireless in first 9M\nNov 15, 2021\nLATEST ARTICLES\nNews\nSubsea cables are critical infra requiring whole-of-nation protection – PLDT\nOct 14, 2026\nMalasakit (ESG)\nPLDT, Smart and Unilab Foundation bring crisis-tested learning program to more Philippine schools\nOct 13, 2026\nNews\nPLDT Global and Smart extend support to Filipinos in Saudi Arabia amid ongoing incident\nOct 13, 2026\nNews\nPLDT Group’s ERICA Wins 2026 AIBP Enterprise Innovation Award for Data and AI\nOct 9, 2026","domain":"main.pldt.com","id":2110626010797051904,"post_ts":1633536000000,"ss":[{"chunk_id":0,"content":"Innovation\nDynamic learning, cybersecurity top bill PLDT, Smart innovations for school year\nOct 7, 2021\nPLDT and wireless unit Smart Communications, Inc. are boosting e-learning in the new school year with two new courses on the Innovations Academy for Disaster Awareness, Preparedness, and Training (iADAPT) platform.","ctx":{"span":[0,317]}},{"chunk_id":1,"content":"Powered by the Philippine Disaster Resilience Foundation, iADAPT houses interactive courses developed by industry leaders on risk reduction and management, business continuity, and climate change adaptation.","ctx":{"span":[0,206]}},{"chunk_id":2,"content":"This school year, two new e-learning courses, the CyberSmart and the Central Visayan Institute Foundation-Dynamic Learning Program (CVIF-DLP) will be made available to Smart partner schools and the Department of Education (DepEd) divisions on the iADAPT platform. The first 300 registrants on the site will be able to access the courses for free.","ctx":{"span":[0,345]}},{"chunk_id":3,"content":"“The new school year presents new challenges for students and teachers as they continue education through blended learning. Smart offers innovative programs that ensure no learner is left behind and protect Filipinos against online threats as they rely on the internet for school and work,” said Stephanie V. Orlino, Smart Assistant Vice President and Head of Community Relations.","ctx":{"span":[0,379]}},{"chunk_id":4,"content":"Orlino, Smart Assistant Vice President and Head of Community Relations. Learn Smart and Work Smart at home Centered around the CyberSmart Investigation Agency, the cybersecurity course includes topics on online child safety, data privacy and security, gadget protection, spotting and combating fake news, and responsible use of social media, as well as digital wellbeing and mental","ctx":{"span":[0,380]}},{"chunk_id":5,"content":"health.","ctx":{"span":[0,6]}},{"chunk_id":6,"content":"health. CyberSmart is a collaboration between various business units across PLDT and Smart. It is supported by the DepEd, the National Privacy Commission, UNICEF, International Justice Mission, and Internet Watch Foundation..","ctx":{"span":[0,224]}},{"chunk_id":7,"content":"Pandemic-resilient education program\nAccredited by the DepEd as a supplementary resource, the CVIF-DLP works well with blended learning whether students are at home or in a limited face-to-face setting. The program develops them into independent learners through the self-directed CVIF-DLP Learning Activity Sheets (CVIF-DLP LAS).","ctx":{"span":[0,329]}},{"chunk_id":8,"content":"PLDT, Smart, and the PLDT-Smart Foundation have backed the crisis-resilient teaching method developed by renowned Filipino Theoretical Physicists and Ramon Magsaysay Awardees for Education Dr. Christopher Bernido and Dr. Ma. Victoria Carpio-Bernido since 2010.","ctx":{"span":[0,259]}},{"chunk_id":9,"content":"Victoria Carpio-Bernido since 2010. So far, Smart has trained over 13,800 teachers in 753 public and private schools and five alternative learning system divisions and helped produce 2,235 CVIF-DLP LAS free to download at the DepEd Commons.","ctx":{"span":[0,239]}},{"chunk_id":10,"content":"PLDT and Smart foster learning through technology to help the nation achieve the United Nation’s Sustainable Development Goal (SDG) #4: Quality Education. Check out PLDT and Smart learning materials at https://iadapt.pdrf.org/SMART.","ctx":{"span":[0,231]}},{"chunk_id":11,"content":"RELATED ARTICLES Innovation PLDT and Smart support United Nations-led ethical AI agenda Dec 20, 2023 Innovation PLDT Breaks Ground for 11th and Largest Hyperscale Data Center Mar 18, 2022 Innovation J.A.R.V.I.S.-like program for business wins PLDT, Smart startup tilt Nov 22, 2021 Innovation PLDT champions startups, widens search for innovations Nov 18, 2021 Innovation PLDT, Smart","ctx":{"span":[0,381]}},{"chunk_id":12,"content":"outpace competition in fiber, mobile, fixed wireless in first 9M Nov 15, 2021 LATEST ARTICLES News Subsea cables are critical infra requiring whole-of-nation protection – PLDT Oct 14, 2026 Malasakit 